/*
  UserImpersonateButton.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0050 · UserImpersonateButton (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `UserImpersonateButton` resolves (table "UserImpersonateButton") lives here with
  its web `t(key, default)` English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  The first group is the exact keys extracted from the web source
  (features/admin/components/UserImpersonateButton.tsx) — the button labels, the
  aria label, and the ConfirmDialog props. The web i18next `{{subject}}`
  interpolation is expressed natively as `%@` (resolved with `String(format:)`).
  The remaining keys back the native-only chrome (freshness chip, banners, status
  load states, unavailable notes, start feedback) the state list requires.
*/

